41
00:02:05,203 --> 00:02:11,024
So Google came up with this, and they
said if you must measure four signals

42
00:02:11,854 --> 00:02:15,564
about your user-facing systems, these
are the four you should focus on.

43
00:02:16,244 --> 00:02:20,604
And they are latency, which tells you
how long it takes to serve a request.

44
00:02:22,594 --> 00:02:24,684
There's error that tells you
the rate of requests that fail.

45
00:02:25,394 --> 00:02:29,054
Traffic lets you know how much demand
is being placed on your system.

46
00:02:29,573 --> 00:02:33,794
Saturation tells you how full your system
is, how much of your resources are being

47
00:02:33,794 --> 00:02:35,914
used up, and how quickly they can run out.

48
00:02:36,914 --> 00:02:37,454
Excuse me.

49
00:02:38,914 --> 00:02:44,713
So what do these signals tell you
about the health of your system?

50
00:02:44,714 --> 00:02:47,253
Like, why do we need
to monitor the signals?

51
00:02:47,894 --> 00:02:51,254
There are a couple of reasons
why we monitor them, and one of

52
00:02:51,254 --> 00:02:54,644
them is that they measure what
the user actually experiences.

53
00:02:54,654 --> 00:02:56,513
So it's user it's user-focused.

54
00:02:56,983 --> 00:02:58,974
Let's take latency, for instance.

55
00:02:59,264 --> 00:02:59,424
You are measuring latency.

56
00:02:59,424 --> 00:03:04,443
Latency tells you how long it takes for a
user request that's in engineering terms.

57
00:03:05,064 --> 00:03:09,663
But on user end, it's, Translates
or it appears as a lag.

58
00:03:09,953 --> 00:03:11,543
So it's a slow responding page.

59
00:03:11,563 --> 00:03:13,923
I go to your landing page and it
takes a long time for it to load.

60
00:03:15,223 --> 00:03:16,303
That's frustrating for the user.

61
00:03:17,193 --> 00:03:21,633
And so that's one of the reasons why we
measure latency, to help you know what

62
00:03:22,563 --> 00:03:24,133
the user is experiencing on their own end.

63
00:03:25,453 --> 00:03:31,673
So the second reason is it helps
you detect problems early on.

64
00:03:32,523 --> 00:03:33,192
Performance drops and failures before
users start complaining about them.

65
00:03:33,192 --> 00:03:33,498
It helps you

66
00:03:34,498 --> 00:03:37,448
troubleshoot faster, they lower
the time that it takes to detect

67
00:03:37,448 --> 00:03:41,138
and fix system issues, and also
helps you with capacity planning.

68
00:03:41,148 --> 00:03:43,678
You'll be able to predict when
your system will run out of

69
00:03:43,678 --> 00:03:44,698
resources under heavy load.

